1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,151
VAR can't review everything.

2
00:00:02,746 --> 00:00:04,370
It only steps in for four kinds

3
00:00:04,182 --> 00:00:04,949
of decision.

4
00:00:05,810 --> 00:00:07,098
Goal or no goal.

5
00:00:07,693 --> 00:00:09,235
Penalty or no penalty.

6
00:00:09,834 --> 00:00:11,168
Direct red card.

7
00:00:11,767 --> 00:00:13,182
And mistaken identity:

8
00:00:13,179 --> 00:00:15,115
when the referee books the wrong player.

9
00:00:15,978 --> 00:00:17,521
A foul in midfield that leads to

10
00:00:17,332 --> 00:00:17,984
nothing?

11
00:00:18,578 --> 00:00:20,850
Not reviewable, however wrong the call.

12
00:00:21,730 --> 00:00:23,319
And even then, it has to be

13
00:00:23,130 --> 00:00:24,685
a clear and obvious error.

14
00:00:25,538 --> 00:00:27,034
Players can't ask for it.

15
00:00:27,629 --> 00:00:29,577
Only the referee can start a review,

16
00:00:29,562 --> 00:00:31,325
and making the screen gesture risks a

17
00:00:31,136 --> 00:00:32,146
yellow card.

18
00:00:33,018 --> 00:00:34,618
And VAR doesn't decide:

19
00:00:34,615 --> 00:00:35,649
it recommends.

20
00:00:36,243 --> 00:00:38,284
The final decision always belongs to the

21
00:00:38,095 --> 00:00:38,886
referee.

22
00:00:39,754 --> 00:00:40,822
New this edition:

23
00:00:40,807 --> 00:00:42,836
a clearly incorrect second yellow can now

24
00:00:42,647 --> 00:00:43,530
be reviewed.

25
00:00:44,402 --> 00:00:46,257
Save it, and share it with whoever

26
00:00:46,069 --> 00:00:47,993
screams for VAR every week.

